message: "If you use this architecture, code or results, please cite the technical report."
title: "A Brain That Is Never Switched Off: Binary Neurons, One Local Learning Rule, Innate Wiring and Speech Only Through Muscles"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Zhiwen
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-8289-6393"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
repository-code: "https://github.com/leeR1ven/concept-brain"
url: "https://github.com/leeR1ven/concept-brain"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-11-09"
abstract: >-
  A research prototype of an artificial brain that lives one continuous life: binary neurons wired at birth by one
  generator, one local Hebbian learning rule with concave growth and one global decay, output only through muscles.
  A multi-layer prefrontal cortex predicts the next input; a thought is a first-layer copy lit from inside; speaking is
  that prediction returned to the muscles. In an invented logic language the brain learns by only listening to
  dialogues, with no reward, once sentences fit its working-memory window, and answers in turn without talking over
  others.
keywords:
  - brain-inspired architecture
  - Hebbian learning
  - continual learning
  - binary neurons
  - prefrontal cortex
  - working memory
  - language learning
